  "id": "COMPOUND:29877 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "Pestaloficiol A appears to have a shared target relationship with SNU-387 through a common intermediate molecule, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This molecule acts as a bridge, with Pestaloficiol A directly targeting SK-VLB, A2780cisR, or KB, all of which are targets of the same compound. The evidence suggests that Pestaloficiol A may exert its biological effect through a mechanism that involves the activation of this intermediate, which in turn influences SNU-387. The consistent presence of this intermediate in all three pathways supports a unified pathway where Pestaloficiol A's activity is mediated by a shared molecular interaction. The evidence does not provide direct evidence of a direct interaction between Pestaloficiol A and SNU-387, but rather through a chain of targets, suggesting a potential role in a broader signaling network.",
